<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The PST reader (§7.7), built in-house from the published [MS-PST] specification. Read-only
    by stated scope: almost nothing writes this format, but someone arriving from it has their
    mail inside one and this is how it gets out.

    Three layers, mirroring the specification's own: NDB (nodes, blocks, the two BTrees and the
    obfuscation), LTP (heaps, property and table contexts), and messaging (folders, messages,
    attachments). No dependencies on purpose — a parser for somebody else's binary format is an
    attack surface (§19), and the fewer moving parts under it the better. Every structure is
    verified against the specification's own worked byte examples, and the whole stack against
    real files this project did not write.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Mailbox.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
